WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.834 --> 00:00:06.920
Did you know

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:11.800
that an estimated 10 million children
in the United States

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:15.845
see their fathers less than once a month?

00:00:17.556 --> 00:00:23.603
Research tells us what happens
to boys and girls without dads

00:00:23.603 --> 00:00:25.897
or stable father figures in their lives.

00:00:26.982 --> 00:00:29.109
Poverty rates double,

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:33.405
emotional and behavioral
health issues increase,

00:00:33.446 --> 00:00:39.411
high school dropout rates increase,
as do crime and prison rates.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.330
And I was no different.

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:46.293
I grew up in Georgia without my father.

00:00:47.752 --> 00:00:49.296
My mother raised me.

00:00:50.171 --> 00:00:52.966
And let me tell you
something about my mom.

00:00:54.134 --> 00:00:58.013
Every day before school, she would look
me in the eyes and say to me,

00:00:58.054 --> 00:01:02.642
"You are tall, dark and handsome."

00:01:02.642 --> 00:01:05.228
(Laughter)

00:01:05.687 --> 00:01:10.609
(Applause)

00:01:11.151 --> 00:01:14.654
"And you can do anything
you want in this world

00:01:14.654 --> 00:01:16.531
if you put your mind to it."

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:20.619
But I didn't believe her.

00:01:23.246 --> 00:01:24.623
I struggled.

00:01:27.083 --> 00:01:29.336
Behavioral issues,

00:01:29.377 --> 00:01:31.921
substance abuse issues,

00:01:31.921 --> 00:01:33.882
suicidal ideation.

00:01:34.966 --> 00:01:38.470
I blamed myself
for my father being absent.

00:01:42.307 --> 00:01:44.392
I remember I was in college.

00:01:45.268 --> 00:01:48.396
In my room by myself.

00:01:49.314 --> 00:01:53.151
"God, you have to help me use my pain."

00:01:54.069 --> 00:01:56.780
So I went on a journey to find my father.

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:59.866
And what I found was shocking.

00:02:01.409 --> 00:02:05.914
My father had been experiencing an issue
that he needed help in overcoming.

00:02:07.499 --> 00:02:09.918
He was experiencing his own pain.

00:02:11.961 --> 00:02:15.757
His absence was not my fault.

00:02:16.132 --> 00:02:18.802
And in a way, not his fault.

00:02:19.969 --> 00:02:21.930
Then I thought to myself,

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:25.433
what if my father would have had
a caring group of neighbors

00:02:25.475 --> 00:02:26.810
to support him?

00:02:27.519 --> 00:02:30.021
It would have made a difference
for the both of us.

00:02:31.773 --> 00:02:36.194
Now, there's a lot of reasons that keep
fathers separated from their children.

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:40.240
There are the ones
you might think of right away,

00:02:40.281 --> 00:02:42.575
like estrangement from a mother,

00:02:42.617 --> 00:02:47.330
substance abuse, sickness
and incarceration.

00:02:48.957 --> 00:02:52.544
But the reasons that don't get
talked about enough

00:02:52.585 --> 00:02:55.839
are the ones that exacerbate the problem.

00:02:57.090 --> 00:03:01.052
Those are the emotions
we don't talk about enough.

00:03:02.887 --> 00:03:05.390
I'm talking about shame.

00:03:06.599 --> 00:03:07.767
Guilt.

00:03:08.852 --> 00:03:10.311
And embarrassment.

00:03:12.355 --> 00:03:17.527
These emotions can cause so much harm

00:03:17.569 --> 00:03:19.863
beyond the absence.

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:27.996
Ben was a 32-year-old father

00:03:28.037 --> 00:03:31.166
at an agency that I run
called Fathers’ UpLift,

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:36.629
where we help fathers love,
forgive and heal.

00:03:37.005 --> 00:03:38.339
And in doing so,

00:03:38.381 --> 00:03:42.927
they learn to find the beauty
in the pain they've experienced.

00:03:44.763 --> 00:03:48.099
Now one might ask,
how can pain be beautiful?

00:03:49.768 --> 00:03:53.062
At Fathers' UpLift, we believe
that pain gives you character,

00:03:53.104 --> 00:03:55.398
strength and courage.

00:03:56.149 --> 00:03:59.569
More importantly, there is a mystery
on the other side of pain.

00:04:00.904 --> 00:04:03.072
For the population we work with,

00:04:03.072 --> 00:04:05.742
that mystery is a father's child.

00:04:07.202 --> 00:04:12.874
The warm embrace with your child
on the other side of the mystery,

00:04:12.916 --> 00:04:14.250
that is beauty.

00:04:16.711 --> 00:04:20.298
Ben spent four years
separated from his child

00:04:20.298 --> 00:04:23.927
due to co-parenting issues.

00:04:23.968 --> 00:04:26.221
restraining orders

00:04:26.262 --> 00:04:28.723
and challenges navigating
the family court.

00:04:29.933 --> 00:04:32.477
But he also experienced shame

00:04:32.519 --> 00:04:35.855
from not being able
to see his daughter daily,

00:04:35.855 --> 00:04:38.274
guilt because he was absent

00:04:38.316 --> 00:04:42.612
and embarrassment because he was unable
to spend time with his daughter

00:04:42.654 --> 00:04:44.781
on a consistent basis.

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:50.119
Now it is imperative to note

00:04:50.119 --> 00:04:53.414
that as we stand here today,

00:04:53.456 --> 00:04:58.503
that through prior relationships
men learn to love and hate.

00:05:00.129 --> 00:05:03.049
Some of us have limited
experience with love.

00:05:04.217 --> 00:05:08.972
Therefore, relationships
that emphasize self-love

00:05:09.013 --> 00:05:11.808
play an essential role in the work we do.

00:05:13.101 --> 00:05:16.604
Lifelong relationships
are integral to our efforts,

00:05:16.646 --> 00:05:19.983
with specific emphasis
on an individual's ability

00:05:20.024 --> 00:05:23.486
to mirror new behavior and connections.

00:05:25.238 --> 00:05:28.867
Now, while many fathers like Ben
come to our agency

00:05:28.908 --> 00:05:32.954
through social service agencies
and correctional facilities,

00:05:32.954 --> 00:05:36.499
many of them come to us
through word of mouth.

00:05:38.042 --> 00:05:41.796
They come to our clinic
and can work one-on-one

00:05:41.838 --> 00:05:44.465
with a licensed therapist and coach.

00:05:45.508 --> 00:05:49.429
A team of individuals
that provide guidance,

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:52.181
advocacy and mentorship.

00:05:53.391 --> 00:05:55.268
We also offer group therapy.

00:05:56.477 --> 00:06:00.231
In groups of five to 25 fathers or more,

00:06:00.273 --> 00:06:03.735
they share stories about their children
and comfort one another

00:06:03.776 --> 00:06:06.696
as they work to achieve a common goal.

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:10.700
They hear stories of triumph and struggle

00:06:10.742 --> 00:06:14.120
and pour into one another
whenever there is a need.

00:06:14.996 --> 00:06:18.166
Together, we ensure
that fathers are mentally

00:06:18.207 --> 00:06:21.711
and emotionally prepared
to be in their children's lives.

00:06:22.086 --> 00:06:24.380
And when their father
has achieved his goal,

00:06:24.422 --> 00:06:27.175
he is invited to come back
and be an ambassador

00:06:27.175 --> 00:06:28.718
and pay it forward.

00:06:29.594 --> 00:06:32.805
And last but not least,

00:06:32.805 --> 00:06:36.142
we ensure that mental health providers,

00:06:36.184 --> 00:06:38.686
universities and institutions

00:06:38.728 --> 00:06:43.524
have the tools they need to engage fathers
wherever they are throughout the world,

00:06:43.566 --> 00:06:45.902
through our online
and in-person instruction.

00:06:46.653 --> 00:06:51.783
(Applause)

00:06:53.242 --> 00:06:56.204
We work with fathers
as long as they need us.

00:06:56.704 --> 00:07:00.249
Or, in other words, until they fire us.

00:07:00.249 --> 00:07:02.418
(Laughter)

00:07:02.877 --> 00:07:06.089
Now there is no easy formula here.

00:07:07.382 --> 00:07:09.050
Every dad is different.

00:07:09.676 --> 00:07:11.344
Every kid is different.

00:07:12.011 --> 00:07:13.721
Every story is different.

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:17.141
But there are a few things
we do every time.

00:07:17.642 --> 00:07:21.354
We are loving our fathers
and the fatherless back to life.

00:07:22.563 --> 00:07:26.943
(Applause)

00:07:27.485 --> 00:07:29.112
We hug our fathers.

00:07:30.446 --> 00:07:33.866
We celebrate them on birthdays
and holidays with a call

00:07:33.908 --> 00:07:37.036
to let them know how much
we appreciate them.

00:07:37.578 --> 00:07:41.499
And we assume that they have
the power to achieve their goals.

00:07:42.083 --> 00:07:45.503
We are a consistent
source of support for them

00:07:45.503 --> 00:07:49.924
as they work to process the mistakes
they've made in the past.

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:57.098
For the last few years, we’ve served
over 10,000 fathers in their families.

00:07:57.974 --> 00:08:03.521
(Applause)

00:08:04.522 --> 00:08:07.025
We've seen fathers accomplish goals,

00:08:07.066 --> 00:08:10.862
such as gaining shared custody
of their children,

00:08:10.862 --> 00:08:13.197
loving themselves again

00:08:13.239 --> 00:08:15.908
and gaining a newfound appreciation

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:18.995
for everything they have
experienced in their life.

00:08:21.456 --> 00:08:24.417
All of our fathers enter our doors
feeling hopeless.

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:26.878
But when they leave,

00:08:26.878 --> 00:08:30.590
over 90 percent of them say
they have an improved sense of identity

00:08:30.631 --> 00:08:31.841
and self-worth.

00:08:31.883 --> 00:08:34.719
We've helped fathers
released from jail and prison

00:08:34.761 --> 00:08:38.973
return home with their worth,
their dignity and their self-respect.

00:08:39.807 --> 00:08:44.270
(Applause)

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:47.815
And of course,

00:08:47.815 --> 00:08:50.359
our work just doesn't benefit fathers.

00:08:51.903 --> 00:08:53.654
It's for the kids too.

00:08:54.489 --> 00:08:57.992
A kid blaming himself for something
he doesn't understand.

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:03.623
The kid like I was, who struggled

00:09:03.664 --> 00:09:07.502
and who didn't understand
that fathers are human too.

00:09:12.381 --> 00:09:17.220
My father's absence inspired me to create
a safe haven for fathers nationwide.

00:09:18.596 --> 00:09:20.598
And truth be told,

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:23.643
my father is currently leading
a life separated from me

00:09:23.684 --> 00:09:25.228
as we speak today.

00:09:26.562 --> 00:09:29.357
Unfortunately, it is not a perfect ending.

00:09:30.483 --> 00:09:32.401
But it is an important one.

00:09:33.361 --> 00:09:36.614
It sheds light on the fact
that fathers hurt too.

00:09:36.614 --> 00:09:42.870
And it is our responsibility to love them
back to life whenever the need exist.

00:09:47.416 --> 00:09:50.545
As I stand on the stage,

00:09:50.586 --> 00:09:54.382
I can't stop thinking
about my seven-year-old son, Clayton,

00:09:54.423 --> 00:09:57.051
and my one-year-old daughter,
SaMya Grace.

00:09:58.511 --> 00:10:01.806
The other day, I asked Clayton,

00:10:01.848 --> 00:10:03.641
"What kind of father am I?"

00:10:05.268 --> 00:10:07.228
He looked at me and said,

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:09.689
"Um, you have a mustache,"

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:12.150
(Laughter)

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:14.902
"Long hair," this was before
the haircut, may I add.

00:10:14.944 --> 00:10:16.487
(Laughter)

00:10:16.529 --> 00:10:18.030
"And even a new computer."

00:10:19.699 --> 00:10:21.534
I was like, "OK, this is true, son."

00:10:23.744 --> 00:10:26.289
He goes on to say,

00:10:26.289 --> 00:10:29.292
"I love it when you buy me games,"
before hugging me --

00:10:29.292 --> 00:10:31.961
(Laughter)

00:10:32.003 --> 00:10:33.629
And running back to his room.

00:10:33.629 --> 00:10:34.797
(Laughter)

00:10:36.716 --> 00:10:38.217
And SaMya Grace.

00:10:39.468 --> 00:10:41.971
Every time I ask her for a kiss,

00:10:42.013 --> 00:10:46.934
she puckers up her lips and she runs
to kiss me with an enormous smile.

00:10:50.021 --> 00:10:51.898
That makes my day every time.

00:10:53.816 --> 00:10:55.276
When moments like these occur,

00:10:55.318 --> 00:10:58.613
I understand that I have
the privilege to be present,

00:10:58.613 --> 00:11:02.742
unlike many of the fathers that walk
through our doors for the first time.

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:06.662
Like them, I am far from perfect.

00:11:08.664 --> 00:11:11.834
Despite my mistakes,

00:11:11.834 --> 00:11:15.338
my greatest achievement
is being Clayton and SaMya's father.

00:11:17.256 --> 00:11:22.136
(Applause)

00:11:22.887 --> 00:11:26.974
Millions of fathers today,

00:11:26.974 --> 00:11:29.936
regardless of their location,

00:11:29.977 --> 00:11:31.646
can say the same thing.

00:11:35.191 --> 00:11:38.236
I must admit,

00:11:38.236 --> 00:11:40.863
if it had not been
for the individuals in my life

00:11:40.905 --> 00:11:44.116
that reminded me of how valuable I was,

00:11:44.116 --> 00:11:45.826
I would not be here today.

00:11:46.661 --> 00:11:50.164
I'm more than thankful for them
that they loved me back to life.

00:11:51.958 --> 00:11:57.129
Fathers that have been absent,
regardless of their past mistakes,

00:11:57.171 --> 00:11:58.881
deserve a lifeline.

00:11:59.215 --> 00:12:02.301
And if we are deserving,

00:12:02.343 --> 00:12:04.845
so are the ones who have lost their way.

00:12:07.932 --> 00:12:09.558
Take a moment with me.

00:12:10.309 --> 00:12:11.602
Fifteen seconds.

00:12:12.478 --> 00:12:14.146
And I'll keep the time.

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:19.318
Think about the people who loved you
when you lost your way.

00:12:21.904 --> 00:12:23.698
Who huged you when you needed it.

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:27.910
Who assumed best intention.

00:12:30.162 --> 00:12:31.956
Who validated you.

00:12:32.415 --> 00:12:35.501
And embraced you
even when you felt undeserving.

00:12:37.586 --> 00:12:39.380
Whoever came to mind,

00:12:39.422 --> 00:12:44.051
try, just try and be that to someone else.

00:12:44.051 --> 00:12:45.219
Thank you.

00:12:45.219 --> 00:12:51.559
(Applause)

